      "writtenOn": "2021-01-08T19:53:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we have multiple measurements per RAN? If so, we\u0027ll need to sort by Comparator.comparingInt(SigThreshInfo::getRANType).thenComparingInt(SigThreshInfo::getSignalMeasurement).\n\nIt\u0027s hard to tell from the docs what the expected support for multiple measurements per RAN is:\n\n1.2 is fairly clear, I read this as \"only one measurement per RAN is allowed if precise dB thresholds are set\":\nNote: As this mechanism generally only constrains reports based on one measured quantity per RAN, if multiple measured quantities must be used to trigger a report for a given RAN, the only valid field may be hysteresisMs: hysteresisDb and thresholdsDbm must be set to zero and length zero respectively.\n\n1.5 is much less clear IMO, but I think it\u0027s trying to say the same thing as 1.2?:\nFor each RAN, if any of reporting criteria of any measure is set enabled, the reporting criteria of the other measures in this RAN are set disabled (see @1.5::SignalThresholdInfo.isEnabled) until they are set enabled.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 83,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 83,
        "endChar": 87
      },
      "revId": "f3fe21f31e8d65da5fc926e16856988753d946dd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
